# Mining Game — UI Design & Motion Rules

Apply this design and motion system to the project's existing UI and to any future UI that is **explicitly requested**.

**Do not create new UI, screens, panels, systems, features, or components unless a separate instruction explicitly asks for them.**

## Scope
- Visual and motion standard only
- When touching existing UI: preserve functionality, hierarchy, bindings, logic, navigation, and content unless told otherwise
- Only restyle or animate what already exists

## Visual identity
**near-black industrial UI + transparent glass + cyan/blue neon + restrained green highlights + precise technical motion**

Do not introduce other styles. Do not invent new UI structures to satisfy the style.

## Color
- Background / panel fill: near-black / very dark navy, transparent
- Primary accent: electric cyan / blue — navigation, interaction, system info
- Secondary accent: neon green — resources, positive states, success
- Neutral text: cold white / light blue-gray — primary information
- Warning: amber / orange
- Critical: red

Never use arbitrary accents.

## Panels
Transparent technical displays: thin 1–2px borders, subtle cyan edge light, angular/chamfered corners, thin dividers, small corner brackets, very subtle scan-line/grid. Readable over gameplay.

Avoid: large opaque rectangles, rounded cards, pills, mobile/SaaS styling, excessive decoration.

## Glow
Subtle, controlled — active borders, selection, progress, important values, warnings. Never panel-wide bloom or heavy blur.

## Typography
Technical / industrial: uppercase headings, short labels, strong numeric readouts, compact spacing. Values dominate labels. Prefer monospaced feel for data when practical.

## Shape language
Rectangles, angular cuts, chamfers, thin lines, brackets, segmented bars. Avoid soft circles/curves unless gauges require them.

## Buttons
Machine controls: transparent dark fill, subtle border, low cyan detail. Hover = brighter border + slight fill. Press = quick brightness/compression. Selected = persistent accent line/marker. Disabled = reduced opacity, almost no glow. Never large glowing rectangles.

## HUD layout
Keep center clear. Permanent info at corners/edges. Group visually; primary high contrast, secondary quieter, tertiary very low intensity.

## Motion
Fast, controlled, precise, subtle, mechanical. No bounce/elastic/overshoot.

Timing (approx): hover 80–120ms · press 60–100ms · small state 100–160ms · panel 180–280ms · large screen 250–400ms · ambient slow/subtle.

Panel enter: fade + 8–24px slide + border illuminate + content then secondary details. Exit slightly faster. Data readouts: brief emphasize on change, optional short count — not continuous animation. Scanner: thin scan lines, sweeps, expanding rings — never large opaque animated graphics.

## Unity constraints
Implement with practical uGUI / UI Toolkit / IMGUI / lightweight sprites/materials. Prefer transparent panels, sliced borders, masks, simple gradients. Avoid expensive realtime blur as core identity.

## Reusable components (when UI creation is explicitly requested)
Reuse established styles: CyberPanel, CyberButton, CyberIconButton, CyberTab, StatReadout, ProgressBar, SegmentedBar, WarningIndicator, ResourceRow, UpgradeCard, SectionHeader, Tooltip, ModalPanel.

## World overlays (scan / radar)
Hairline neon strokes; soft vector outline zones for scan estimates; quiet transparency. Same industrial cyber language.

## Priority
**clarity → hierarchy → consistency → responsiveness → atmosphere**

When uncertain: simpler and more consistent.
